Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 02:21:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Optionally Desugar static methods in interface

Why

dx requires min-sdk>=24 to support default methods in
interface.otherwise convertion would be failed.

```
WARNING in com.genymobile.scrcpy.model.Codec.getMimeType:(Landroid/media/MediaCodec;)Ljava/lang/String;: defining a static interface method requires --min-sdk-version >= 24 (currently 13) for interface methods: com.genymobile.scrcpy.model.Codec.getMimeType:(Landroid/media/MediaCodec;)Ljava/lang/String;
Uncaught translation error: com.android.dx.cf.code.SimException: ERROR in com.genymobile.scrcpy.audio.AudioEncoder.createMediaCodec:(Lcom/genymobile/scrcpy/model/Codec;Ljava/lang/String;)Landroid/media/MediaCodec;: invoking a static interface method com.genymobile.scrcpy.model.Codec.getMimeType:(Landroid/media/MediaCodec;)Ljava/lang/String; strictly requires --min-sdk-version >= 24 (blocked at current API level 13)
Uncaught translation error: com.android.dx.cf.code.SimException: ERROR in com.genymobile.scrcpy.video.SurfaceEncoder.createMediaCodec:(Lcom/genymobile/scrcpy/model/Codec;Ljava/lang/String;)Landroid/media/MediaCodec;: invoking a static interface method com.genymobile.scrcpy.model.Codec.getMimeType:(Landroid/media/MediaCodec;)Ljava/lang/String; strictly requires --min-sdk-version >= 24 (blocked at current API level 13)
```

If you call dx with --min-sdk-version >= 24, on device (sdk<24) it will show unknown dex version (dex version
updated form sdk>=24).

```
W art     : Failed to open dex file '/data/local/tmp/scrcpy-server.jar' from memory: Unrecognized version number in /data/local/tmp/scrcpy-server.jar: 0 3 7
E appproc : ERROR: could not find class 'com.genymobile.scrcpy.Server'
```

To support the same version range as upstream build and README
(minsdk>=21),we must remove static methods in interface.

d8 desugar default interface methods to companion classes

What we do

manullay create nested class in interface which contains default
methods and rewrite all call to the default methods.

How to find which to fix
1. see dx complains
2. find `static` keyword in interfaces

Alternative way:

Use dx --allow-all-interface-method-invokes and --min-sdk-version=21 is ok, it will just show warning, but allow to convert.
(and runtime is ok, tested on an Android 6.0.1 device)
Although it is experimental in dx
```
// Experimentally invoke-static of static interface methods
// breaks on VMs running below API level 21. Invocations of
// default interface methods may soft-fail verification but so
// long as they are not called that's okay.
```
So it might be safe to use since we have min sdk >=21

https://android.googlesource.com/platform/dalvik/+/refs/heads/main/dx/src/com/android/dx/cf/code/Simulator.java#884
---
 .../java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/audio/AudioEncoder.java   | 2 +-
 .../src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/model/Codec.java | 9 ++++++---
 .../java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/video/SurfaceEncoder.java | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/audio/AudioEncoder.java b/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/audio/AudioEncoder.java
index 13b7edd0..6d90d3c4 100644
--- a/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/audio/AudioEncoder.java
+++ b/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/audio/AudioEncoder.java
@@ -331,7 +331,7 @@ public final class AudioEncoder implements AsyncProcessor {
             Ln.d("Creating audio encoder by name: '" + encoderName + "'");
             try {
                 MediaCodec mediaCodec = MediaCodec.createByCodecName(encoderName);
-                String mimeType = Codec.getMimeType(mediaCodec);
+                String mimeType = Codec.CC.getMimeType(mediaCodec);
                 if (!codec.getMimeType().equals(mimeType)) {
                     Ln.e("Audio encoder type for \"" + encoderName + "\" (" + mimeType + ") does not match codec type (" + codec.getMimeType() + ")");
                     throw new ConfigurationException("Incorrect encoder type: " + encoderName);
diff --git a/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/model/Codec.java b/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/model/Codec.java
index b1117102..77c857a2 100644
--- a/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/model/Codec.java
+++ b/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/model/Codec.java
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 package com.genymobile.scrcpy.model;
 
 import android.media.MediaCodec;
+import com.genymobile.scrcpy.util.Ln;
 
 public interface Codec {
 
@@ -17,8 +18,10 @@ public interface Codec {
 
     String getMimeType();
 
-    static String getMimeType(MediaCodec codec) {
-        String[] types = codec.getCodecInfo().getSupportedTypes();
-        return types.length > 0 ? types[0] : null;
+    public final class CC {
+        public static String getMimeType(MediaCodec codec) {
+            String[] types = codec.getCodecInfo().getSupportedTypes();
+            return types.length > 0 ? types[0] : null;
+        }
     }
 }
diff --git a/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/video/SurfaceEncoder.java b/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/video/SurfaceEncoder.java
index d47f834f..1b55db37 100644
--- a/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/video/SurfaceEncoder.java
+++ b/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/video/SurfaceEncoder.java
@@ -282,7 +282,7 @@ public class SurfaceEncoder implements AsyncProcessor {
             Ln.d("Creating encoder by name: '" + encoderName + "'");
             try {
                 MediaCodec mediaCodec = MediaCodec.createByCodecName(encoderName);
-                String mimeType = Codec.getMimeType(mediaCodec);
+                String mimeType = Codec.CC.getMimeType(mediaCodec);
                 if (!codec.getMimeType().equals(mimeType)) {
                     Ln.e("Video encoder type for \"" + encoderName + "\" (" + mimeType + ") does not match codec type (" + codec.getMimeType() + ")");
                     throw new ConfigurationException("Incorrect encoder type: " + encoderName);
